Pattern Card — Bottleneck vs Tollbooth

This is an adaptation of Bottleneck Migration.

Previously:

\text{find something every winner needs}.

Nvidia/d-Matrix suggests a stronger variant:

\boxed{\text{own the interface competitors must cross}.}

A bottleneck is scarce capacity.

A tollbooth is an interface or standard through which heterogeneous competitors obtain interoperability.

Examples worth testing—not assuming—include semiconductor lithography, networking/interconnects, payments, app distribution, exchanges, identity, cloud interfaces and logistics networks.

A particularly clean semiconductor specimen is ASML: Reuters reports roughly 94% lithography share and industry adoption of its next-generation High-NA EUV machines despite roughly $400 million machine costs. 

So the Moneyball search space becomes:

\text{Winner prediction}
\rightarrow
\text{Bottleneck prediction}
\rightarrow
\boxed{\text{Interface/tollbooth prediction}}.

The third can sometimes be safer because we don’t have to correctly identify the downstream winner.

Status: LOOKAHEAD-TAINTED.

